<section class="chapter" id="touchpoints">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">3. Core Touchpoints &amp; Message Types</h2>
      <p>
        Define the minimum viable touchpoints that should exist for most roles. Role-specific messages can layer on top of this baseline.
      </p>

      <h3>3.1 Application / Sourcing</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Application confirmation</strong> — immediate, automated, sets timeline expectations.</li>
        <li><strong>Status transparency</strong> — basic “what happens next” process view.</li>
        <li><strong>Early disqualification response</strong> — respectful, quick, clear.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.2 Screen</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Availability request + brief agenda outline.</li>
        <li>Invite includes context, links, and interviewer name.</li>
        <li>Post-screen follow-up: next steps or close-out.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.3 Panel / Onsite</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Prep email (“What to expect”).</li>
        <li>Reminder 24 hours before.</li>
        <li>Same-day logistics note for complex loops.</li>
        <li>Post-interview update: decision, timeline, or “still reviewing.”</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Design principle:</strong> every “wait” in the process should have a corresponding communication — even if it’s “we’re still reviewing.”
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="automation">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">4. Automation vs Human Touchpoints</h2>

      <h3>4.1 Good candidates for automation</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Confirmations and basic status updates</li>
        <li>Availability requests and reminders</li>
        <li>Standard delay / “still here” messages</li>
        <li>Thank-you notes and logistics comms</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.2 Stay human-led when trust is at stake</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>High-priority outreach and exec candidates</li>
        <li>Late-stage feedback conversations</li>
        <li>Offer calls, negotiation, expectation resets</li>
        <li>Complex context or escalations</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="slas">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">5. SLAs, Guardrails &amp; Risk</h2>

      <h3>5.1 Example SLAs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Application → first review:</strong> within 3 business days</li>
        <li><strong>Screen → decision:</strong> within 2 business days</li>
        <li><strong>Panel → decision:</strong> within 5 business days (with at least one update)</li>
        <li><strong>Offer → written doc:</strong> within 24 hours of verbal yes</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.2 Guardrails</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No contradictory automations (status conflicts)</li>
        <li>Quarterly template tone review</li>
        <li>Pause automations for sensitive candidates</li>
        <li>All automated comms visible in ATS timeline</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="metrics">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">6. Metrics &amp; Feedback Loops</h2>

      <h3>6.1 Core journey metrics</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Time-in-stage (median + percentiles)</li>
        <li>Drop-off rate by stage</li>
        <li>Communication coverage (% receiving expected touchpoints)</li>
        <li>Candidate satisfaction where surveys exist</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>6.2 How measurement drives iteration</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Long time-in-stage + low comms coverage → workflow fixes</li>
        <li>Drop-off patterns → message/channel adjustments</li>
        <li>Qual feedback → template tone and expectation setting</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="appendix">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">Appendix — Example Message Library</h2>

      <h3>A.1 Application confirmation</h3>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Subject:</strong> Thanks for applying for [Role] at [Company]<br>
        <strong>Excerpt:</strong> “Thanks for your interest. Our team reviews every application. You can expect an update within [X] business days…”
      </div>

      <h3>A.2 Screen scheduling</h3>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Subject:</strong> Quick intro chat — [Role] at [Company]<br>
        <strong>Excerpt:</strong> “I’d love to connect for a short intro conversation. Here’s a link to my calendar, or reply with a few times…”
      </div>

      <h3>A.3 “We’re still here” during panel review</h3>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Subject:</strong> Quick update on your interviews with [Company]<br>
        <strong>Excerpt:</strong> “We’re still consolidating feedback and expect next steps by [date]. I’ll reach out as soon as we have an update…”
      </div>

      <h3>A.4 Respectful close-out</h3>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Subject:</strong> Update on your application for [Role]<br>
        <strong>Excerpt:</strong> “After review, we’ve decided not to move forward for this role. This reflects the match for this opening rather than your overall experience…”
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
